// github_workflow_run.proto — A GITHUB ACTIONS WORKFLOW RUN AS THE DAEMON
// FOLLOWS IT for a workspace: which run, the subscription that waits on it,
// and the run as it stands. Shared by the workflow-run endpoints
// (SubscribeGithubWorkflowRun, UnsubscribeGithubWorkflowRun,
// ListGithubWorkflowRunSubscriptions) and by the one notice the daemon
// delivers.
//
// ONE NOTICE, AT COMPLETION. A workflow-run subscription exists to tell its
// workspace that one run FINISHED, and nothing else: no queued or started
// notice, no per-job or per-step update, no check update. The notice says the
// workflow's name, the run's conclusion, its head commit and its web address,
// and the subscription ends with it.
//
// THE DAEMON READS, THE AGENT IS TOLD, as for a pull request: the daemon
// reads the run on its pull-request cadence through the user's `gh` login,
// and a workspace never polls `gh run view` itself. A read missed while the
// daemon was down is made up by the next one, so a completion is told late,
// never lost.
//
// TOLD ONCE. The subscription is removed in the same transaction that owes
// its completion notice, so a run is never told twice to one subscription,
// and a run that completed is never left followed.

